From: At30c <At30c@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sched/ems: port adaptive fmax from the S5E9965 EMS

The Galaxy S26+ EMS keeps each cluster below its maximum frequency in the
everyday emstune sets and lifts the ceiling in the boost and game sets
(adaptive fmax). Port the idea to the Exynos 990 emstune: a set may carry
an fmax node with one ceiling per coregroup, in kHz (0 = none). Sets that
do not override it inherit the mode's default set, like every other field.

The ceiling is applied as a PM QoS max request on PM_QOS_CLUSTER0..2_FREQ_MAX
from a work item, since sets can change with emstune_mode_lock held and PM
QoS may sleep. Thermal and other max requests still combine with it.
/sys/kernel/ems/emstune/fmax_enabled turns it off at runtime and cur_set
shows the active ceilings.

Replace the fixed 2.21 GHz cap of the Mongoose cluster (DT max-freq) with
this: normal, power-scenario, light-video, balance and pinned cap the big
cluster at 2.21 GHz in their default, med and touch boost sets; their big
boost sets (app launch/switch) and the performance, light-game and
game-mode modes run up to 2.73 GHz again.
